# Service Error Handling

Never throw raw `Error()` or return manual HTTP responses. Use NestJS exceptions:

| Exception | When |
|---|---|
| `NotFoundException` | Resource not found |
| `BadRequestException` | Invalid input |
| `ForbiddenException` | Access denied |
| `UnauthorizedException` | Not authenticated |
| `ConflictException` | Duplicate / conflict |
| `InternalServerErrorException` | Unexpected errors |

Repositories catch Prisma errors and rethrow as the exceptions above. Never expose stack traces or DB details in API responses.

```typescript
// Good
throw new NotFoundException('Product not found');
throw new ForbiddenException('You do not own this product');
throw new ConflictException('Email already registered');

// Bad
throw new Error('something went wrong');
```
